/E (I wanted her sitting on something too big to be a fruit anymore, an apple swollen into a small mountain, the way memory swells the things we can't let go of. Beside her, an echo of her younger face watches from the clouds, soft and quiet, close but unreachable. The stars between them are unsettled on purpose, drifting like thoughts that haven't found where to land.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
