1681 0 obj
<<
/Title (There is a particular cruelty in growing older that no one prepares you for: you finally understand the things you needed to hear, but the person who needed to hear them is gone. We write to our younger selves because we cannot reach them any other way, only through paper, only through memory pretending to be a letter. What we offer is not correction. We are not trying to fix who they were or scold them for not knowing better. We are trying to sit beside them, quietly, the way you would sit beside someone in a waiting room, not to change the outcome but to make the waiting less lonely.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1517 0 R
/Next 1793 0 R
>>
