/Title (And maybe that is enough. Maybe the younger self does not need saving, only witnessing. Someone, even a future self, even an imagined one, who finally says: I see what that cost you. I see how hard you tried, even when no one noticed. Growth, after all, is not the erasure of who we were. It is the slow, deliberate act of looking back without flinching, and choosing to forgive the parts of us that didn't know better yet.)
